apter":"Chapter 1: The Engineer"},{"title":"Lead From the Front — Be Seen in the Mud","chapter":"Chapter 2: The Manager"},{"title":"Integrity Is a System, Not a Slogan","chapter":"Chapter 3: The Values"},{"title":"Planning Is 90% of Execution","chapter":"Chapter 4: The Planner"},{"title":"Standards Are Non-Negotiable — Even Under Pressure","chapter":"Chapter 5: The Standards"},{"title":"The Nation's Progress Is Built by Quiet Bureaucrats","chapter":"Chapter 6: The Legacy"}]},{"id":"scrum-sutherland","title":"Scrum: The Art of Doing Twice the Work in Half the Time","author":"Jeff Sutherland","year":2014,"category":"Productivity","cover":"assets/covers/scrum-sutherland.jpg","readTime":"8 min","tagline":"The agile framework that transformed software — and why it works for any team, anywhere.","lessons":[{"title":"Big-Batch Planning Is a Lie","chapter":"Chapter 1: The Way the World Works Is Broken"},{"title":"The Backlog Is the Brain of the Project","chapter":"Chapter 2: The Backlog"},{"title":"Sprints Make Time Your Ally","chapter":"Chapter 3: Sprints"},{"title":"Self-Organizing Teams Beat Command-and-Control","chapter":"Chapter 4: The Team"},{"title":"The Daily Standup Catches Problems While They're Small","chapter":"Chapter 5: Daily Scrum"},{"title":"Review, Retrospective, Repeat — the Improvement Loop","chapter":"Chapter 6: The Retrospective"}]},{"id":"wise-and-otherwise","title":"Wise & Otherwise: A Lifetime of Experience","author":"Sudha Murty","year":2002,"category":"Self-Improvement","cover":"assets/covers/wise-and-otherwise.jpg","readTime":"8 min","tagline":"Fifty short stories from real life — humility, kindness and the quiet wisdom of ordinary people.","lessons":[{"title":"Humility Opens Doors That Talent Cannot","chapter":"Chapter 1: The First Story"},{"title":"Small Kindnesses Compound Into a Life","chapter":"Chapter 2: The Kindness"},{"title":"Pride Costs More Than It Earns","chapter":"Chapter 3: The Pride"},{"title":"Money Reveals Character — Watch How People Handle It","chapter":"Chapter 4: The Money"},{"title":"Family Is the First Classroom of Character","chapter":"Chapter 5: The Family"},{"title":"Service to Others Is the Surest Cure for Self","chapter":"Chapter 6: The Service"}]},{"id":"freakonomics","title":"Freakonomics","author":"Steven D. Levitt & Stephen J. Dubner","year":2005,"category":"Psychology & People","cover":"assets/covers/freakonomics.jpg","readTime":"8 min","tagline":"A rogue economist explores the hidden side of everything — incentives, cheating, crime and the truth nobody says.","lessons":[{"title":"Incentives Rule — Even When We Pretend They Don't","chapter":"Chapter 1: The Hidden Side of Everything"},{"title":"Conventional Wisdom Is Usually Wrong","chapter":"Chapter 2: Conventional Wisdom"},{"title":"The Question Is More Important Than the Answer","chapter":"Chapter 3: Asking the Right Questions"},{"title":"Data Beats Anecdotes — Every Time","chapter":"Chapter 4: The Power of Data"},{"title":"Cheating Is an Incentive Problem, Not a Character Problem","chapter":"Chapter 5: Cheating"},{"title":"The Truth Is Usually Counterintuitive","chapter":"Chapter 6: The Hidden Side of Everything"}]}]
